==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
You should try and bring 2-3 Zombie Killers (such as [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Weedwacker]], [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife]], etc) and wait until the Dread Bore spawns, at which point you want to send something out immediately to get him to burrow. Lure him to the base and spam all of your Zombie Killers (Weedwacker to Freeze, Housewife and Shigong for DPS) and the Dread bore should be taken out before the Project A reaches your stack. If Project A reaches your stack before you kill the Dread Bore, try using the [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] to finish it off. It will drop a lot of money, and just use [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]] and rushers like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] from there to clean up the Project A.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
-

==='''Chapter 3'''===
There are two strategies to approach this stage with - either eliminating Lord Gravey and Cyberhorn with brute force or abuse the Warp-inflicting attacks fired by Gardeneel Bros. to teleport attackers behind the two main threats and finish the base without having to even deal with them. The first obviously requires extreme meatshielding and a fully dedicated formation, while the latter is heavily dependent on precise timing and may result in a few force-quits, as players need to wait until Cyberhorn has advanced sufficiently so units won't be Warped directly into his range.

